<title>PHILIPPINES: Shell's Manila unit cuts unleaded gasoline price.</title>
<headline>Shell's Manila unit cuts unleaded gasoline price.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pilipinas Shell Petroleum Corp said on Thursday it has reduced the price of its unleaded gasoline by 20 centavos per litre to 10.79 pesos effective July 2.</p>
<p>In an advisory, Pilipinas Shell said it lowered the price of unleaded gasoline to reflect decreasing Singapore Posted Prices and world crude oil prices.</p>
<p>Prices of other petroleum products, however, were left unchanged.</p>
<p>The adjustment came two weeks after Shell decreased liquefied petroleum gasoline and diesel prices.</p>
<p>Shell said it would continue to adjust petroleum product prices depending on international and local competition.</p>
<p>Shell, a member of the Royal Dutch/Shell group of companies, is one of three local oil refiners in the Philippines.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom (63 2) 8418939 Fax 8176267</p>
